  "lyrics": [
    {
      "start": 0.05,
      "end": 5.541,
      "text": "An entity is a thing you can describe and tell apart from other things of the same kind.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 5.541,
      "end": 7.375,
      "text": "A customer is an entity.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 7.375,
      "end": 8.958,
      "text": "An order is an entity.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 8.958,
      "end": 10.541,
      "text": "A book is an entity.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 10.541,
      "end": 13.625,
      "text": "Austin is usually not an entity on day one.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 13.625,
      "end": 17.166,
      "text": "It is a value of city, an attribute of customer.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 17.166,
      "end": 19.972,
      "text": "Attributes are facts about one entity.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 19.972,
      "end": 22.708,
      "text": "name, city, joined_on.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 22.708,
      "end": 26.43,
      "text": "If a fact has its own facts, it wanted to be an entity.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 26.43,
      "end": 30.444,
      "text": "city might grow a population, a state, a mayor.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 30.444,
      "end": 35.041,
      "text": "Then city becomes a table, and customers hold city_id.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 35.041,
      "end": 36.791,
      "text": "That promotion is normal.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 36.791,
      "end": 39.361,
      "text": "It is not a mistake in the first sketch.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 39.361,
      "end": 42.555,
      "text": "List nouns from the sentences people actually say.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 42.555,
      "end": 45.097,
      "text": "A customer places an order for a book.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 45.097,
      "end": 46.277,
      "text": "Three nouns.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 46.277,
      "end": 48.583,
      "text": "Then list facts about each noun.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 48.583,
      "end": 51.805,
      "text": "Customer: name, city, email.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 51.805,
      "end": 54.763,
      "text": "Order: placed_on, total.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 54.763,
      "end": 56.527,
      "text": "Book: title, year.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 56.527,
      "end": 58.305,
      "text": "Check one row in your head.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 58.305,
      "end": 60.027,
      "text": "Does it describe one thing?",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 60.027,
      "end": 66.402,
      "text": "If a row describes Maya and also Harbor Light and also a shipping box, you mixed entities.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 66.402,
      "end": 68.902,
      "text": "Split until a row is one noun.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 68.902,
      "end": 71.5,
      "text": "Relationships are not attributes.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 71.5,
      "end": 77.68,
      "text": "customer_id on orders is not a fact about an order in the same way total is.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 77.68,
      "end": 79.888,
      "text": "It is a pointer to another entity.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 79.888,
      "end": 81.652,
      "text": "Keep that difference visible.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 81.652,
      "end": 86.625,
      "text": "Attributes should be atomic for first normal form, which is a later lesson.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 86.625,
      "end": 89.652,
      "text": "For now: one cell, one value.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 89.652,
      "end": 92.444,
      "text": "Not a comma-separated pile of authors.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 92.444,
      "end": 96.013,
      "text": "Derived facts are not attributes you must store.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 96.013,
      "end": 98.861,
      "text": "age can be computed from birth_date.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 98.861,
      "end": 101.569,
      "text": "Storing both is a chance to disagree.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 101.569,
      "end": 103.222,
      "text": "Prefer the source fact.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 103.222,
      "end": 106.597,
      "text": "Names are attributes; identity is a key.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 106.597,
      "end": 109.388,
      "text": "Do not use name as if it were a customer.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 109.388,
      "end": 111.013,
      "text": "Two Mayas exist.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 111.013,
      "end": 114.041,
      "text": "Walk a new domain with sticky notes if you want.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 114.041,
      "end": 115.527,
      "text": "One note per entity.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 115.527,
      "end": 116.819,
      "text": "Facts on the note.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 116.819,
      "end": 118.513,
      "text": "Arrows between notes.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 118.513,
      "end": 120.361,
      "text": "The notes become tables.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 120.361,
      "end": 122.277,
      "text": "The facts become columns.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 122.277,
      "end": 124.236,
      "text": "The arrows become keys.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 124.236,
      "end": 125.916,
      "text": "Events can be entities.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 125.916,
      "end": 128.013,
      "text": "A login is a thing that happened.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 128.013,
      "end": 130.986,
      "text": "It has a time and a customer_id.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 130.986,
      "end": 136.958,
      "text": "It is not an attribute of customer unless you only store last_login_at.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 136.958,
      "end": 141.805,
      "text": "last_login_at is a derived cache of the latest event.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 141.805,
      "end": 143.236,
      "text": "Know which you are building.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 143.236,
      "end": 146.0,
      "text": "Roles can be entities when they have facts.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 146.0,
      "end": 150.208,
      "text": "admin is a flag until admins have offices and rotations.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 150.208,
      "end": 152.027,
      "text": "Then role is a table.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 152.027,
      "end": 158.513,
      "text": "Status values start as text and become entities when they grow labels in three languages.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 158.513,
      "end": 161.972,
      "text": "Promote them when the facts appear, not before.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 161.972,
      "end": 166.083,
      "text": "A good attribute name is a noun or a short noun phrase.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 166.083,
      "end": 169.722,
      "text": "total, placed_at, is_active.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 169.722,
      "end": 172.513,
      "text": "Avoid mystery flags named flag1.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 172.513,
      "end": 177.583,
      "text": "Units belong in the name or in a separate unit column, not in the value.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 177.583,
      "end": 182.388,
      "text": "total_cents versus total dollars as text with a dollar sign.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 182.388,
      "end": 184.291,
      "text": "The first is an attribute.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 184.291,
      "end": 186.027,
      "text": "The second is a poster.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 186.027,
      "end": 188.527,
      "text": "Walk an example row with a skeptic.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 188.527,
      "end": 191.458,
      "text": "If they ask whose city, you mixed entities.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 191.458,
      "end": 194.819,
      "text": "If they ask which of the two titles, you mixed rows.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 194.819,
      "end": 198.291,
      "text": "If they ask what the number means, you mixed attributes.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 198.291,
      "end": 200.68,
      "text": "Fix the mix before you write CREATE.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 200.68,
      "end": 203.069,
      "text": "The sticky notes are cheaper than ALTER.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 203.069,
      "end": 205.958,
      "text": "The nouns were in the sentences all along.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 205.958,
      "end": 207.569,
      "text": "Your job is to hear them.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 207.569,
      "end": 209.791,
      "text": "Design does not start with tables.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 209.791,
      "end": 218.319,
      "text": "It starts with messy speech: we have users, they have payment methods, orders go out, products come back as returns.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 218.319,
      "end": 225.25,
      "text": "Your job is to sort subjects from characteristics, then decide which subjects are entities worth a table.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 225.25,
      "end": 232.263,
      "text": "A subject is a thing you can talk about with a verb: a user has an email, an order contains lines.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 232.263,
      "end": 238.43,
      "text": "A characteristic belongs to a subject: email belongs to user, not to the whole store.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 238.43,
      "end": 241.152,
      "text": "Interview transcripts are full of both.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 241.152,
      "end": 247.333,
      "text": "Highlight nouns that can be the subject of has, contains, places, or belongs to.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 247.333,
      "end": 255.43,
      "text": "Those candidates become entities if they have more than one fact of their own, a lifecycle, and a reason to be found later.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 255.43,
      "end": 263.833,
      "text": "Color might be a characteristic of product, not an entity, until you discover colors have codes, suppliers, and photos.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 263.833,
      "end": 266.125,
      "text": "Then color grew up into an entity.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 266.125,
      "end": 268.43,
      "text": "The test is not the English noun.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 268.43,
      "end": 271.861,
      "text": "The test is whether it has attributes and identity.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 271.861,
      "end": 273.916,
      "text": "Attributes become columns.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 273.916,
      "end": 280.972,
      "text": "Each attribute should be one meaning: email, not contact which mixes phone and email.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 280.972,
      "end": 289.152,
      "text": "If a characteristic repeats as a list in speech \u2014 a user has several payment methods \u2014 it is not a column on users.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 289.274,
      "end": 292.168,
      "text": "It is a second entity related to users.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 292.168,
      "end": 299.71,
      "text": "Ignore noise: adverbs, one-off anecdotes, and attributes nobody will query or constrain.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 299.71,
      "end": 304.654,
      "text": "You can store a note, but you should not invent a table for a sentence said once.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 304.654,
      "end": 311.71,
      "text": "Name entities in the language of the business, then spell them in snake_case when they become tables.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 311.71,
      "end": 313.196,
      "text": "user is an entity.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 313.196,
      "end": 316.418,
      "text": "users is a table if you chose plural tables.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 316.418,
      "end": 319.89,
      "text": "Do not let the sketch and the SQL drift in names.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 319.89,
      "end": 324.279,
      "text": "After you have entities and attributes, you still do not have keys.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 324.279,
      "end": 325.904,
      "text": "Keys are the next lesson.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 325.904,
      "end": 335.376,
      "text": "Here the win is a clean inventory: these are the things, these are the facts about each thing, these lists of facts are actually more things.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 335.376,
      "end": 341.724,
      "text": "If two subjects share a pile of attributes, ask whether they are the same entity in costume.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 341.724,
      "end": 348.599,
      "text": "Customer and user might be one table or two, depending on whether a user can exist without ever buying.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 348.599,
      "end": 352.307,
      "text": "That question is a requirement, not a taste in naming.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 352.307,
      "end": 354.321,
      "text": "Write the entities on boxes.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 354.321,
      "end": 356.154,
      "text": "Write attributes inside.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 356.154,
      "end": 358.876,
      "text": "Leave the lines for the relationship lesson.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 358.876,
      "end": 365.126,
      "text": "A box with twenty attributes is a warning that several subjects are hiding in one list.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 365.126,
      "end": 367.96,
      "text": "Split the box before you draw the first key.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 367.96,
      "end": 374.599,
      "text": "Parse one interview sentence: a user has an account, payment methods, and a cart of products.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 374.599,
      "end": 380.085,
      "text": "Subjects: user, account, payment method, cart, product.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 380.085,
      "end": 388.001,
      "text": "Characteristics: whatever facts they mentioned \u2014 email on user, last four on payment method, quantity in the cart.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 388.001,
      "end": 392.932,
      "text": "Account might be the same as user if login is one-to-one with the person.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 392.932,
      "end": 393.765,
      "text": "Ask.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 393.765,
      "end": 398.099,
      "text": "Cart might be a table of lines, not a column of product names.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 398.099,
      "end": 403.154,
      "text": "Payment methods are many, so not columns card1 card2 on users.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 403.154,
      "end": 408.46,
      "text": "Product is its own entity because it has name, price, manufacturer.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 408.46,
      "end": 414.543,
      "text": "Manufacturer might be text on product until you have manufacturer addresses and contacts.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 414.543,
      "end": 416.029,
      "text": "Then it graduates.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 416.029,
      "end": 420.432,
      "text": "Throw away the word quickly from the interview; it is not an attribute.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 420.432,
      "end": 424.321,
      "text": "Keep email, because uniqueness and login will need it.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 424.321,
      "end": 429.196,
      "text": "This noun work is the whole conversion from real-world ideas to tables.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 429.196,
      "end": 432.529,
      "text": "Tables come after the inventory is honest.",
      "slide": ""
    }
  ]
}
